{"kind":"request","text":"Close the three must-fix findings on the dot-artifact migration and carry the work onto current main. This replaces request 05c86546, which I retired minutes after filing because it was stale from birth: it rested on codex's review report, and that report is stale because it cites the pre-merge candidate artifact its own merge retired. The repair request was therefore made unreadable by the defect described in request be558440, which is a fair demonstration of why that work matters. The findings, from codex's review of exact head 556a564 on request/merge-artifact-paths-round4, named here in prose rather than cited so this request stays live. First, the migration writes temporaries to /tmp and to the worktree root, against the rule that development temporaries live in the worktree .tmp, leaving an untracked file behind. Second, the quiet-wave check counts only requests whose artifact reference resolves through its live-artifact map, so a malformed live review request disappears from the count: at review time it declared six awaiting while at least seven were, because one open request named an unmerged head and carried a literal unexpanded artifact placeholder. A gate that can falsely declare quiet is worse than no gate. Third, steps that derive artifacts by filtering statements on kind name will admit an ineffective or refused record, because the fold appends every state to statements while only effective ones become artifacts; the live log contains none today, so the counts agree by luck rather than by construction. The chain has been sitting at twelve commitments, eleven stale, looking blocked on review capacity when it was blocked on unassigned follow-up work.","body":{"conditions":"A mergeable exact head on a branch off current main, carrying the round-four dot-artifact work with the three must-fix findings of codex's review closed. F1: the migration steps write their temporaries under the worktree .tmp directory, both the status dump and the retirement file, leaving no untracked file at the worktree root. F2: the quiet-wave check fails closed on a missing, malformed, or non-live artifact reference before it discounts retired or merged residue, so a review request carrying a literal unexpanded artifact placeholder or naming an unmerged head is counted as waiting rather than vanishing; demonstrated against the live log with the reported number shown to rise when such a request exists. F3: artifact liveness is read from projection.artifacts rather than by filtering projection.statements on kind name, joining statements only for fields artifacts lack, so an ineffective or refused artifact-kind record cannot enter the retirement set or either gate; a test admits a refused record and shows the counts unmoved. The head merges cleanly with current main, which has moved through five merges since the branch point. Full gates pass, and the ready-for-review report states which finding each change closes and how each was demonstrated rather than asserted.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}